//! Windows 98's and 2000's own 16-color drawings of the pictures Bevel95 draws in their looks
//! (generated by `private/probes/colors16/match`, which finds each True Color picture among the
//! Reference PCs' own files: the 8-bit twin of a 4-bit icon in SHELL32, EXPLORER and MYDOCS, and
//! the toolbars' strips, 98's cut from its screens and 2000's from BROWSEUI.DLL; the report of what
//! matched is beside it). `core::colors16_art` says which True Color picture each one belongs to.
//! The grayed toolbar pictures are made from the plain ones' drawings the way Windows grays a
//! picture (a white copy under a gray one). Rows: '.' see-through, else the color's number among
//! the 16 (`core::colors16::VGA`) in hexadecimal.

